When a traveler from the first village stepped onto the bridge carrying provisions, the bridge would mysteriously triple whatever they carried. But there was a catch: the provisions would appear on the other side, and only a traveler from the second village could decide what to send back across.

At first, villagers sent nothing, fearing loss. The bridge remained empty, and both villages struggled.

